  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Florida's 9th Congressional District election is being contested under dramatically redrawn boundaries approved by Governor Ron DeSantis in May 2026. The new map shifted the district from one where Democrat Kamala Harris won 51% in 2024 to one where Republican Donald Trump would have won over 58%, making the seat a top Republican pickup target. Incumbent Democrat Darren Soto, first elected in 2016 and the first Puerto Rican-American elected to Congress from Florida, is seeking a sixth term in a district that now leans Republican by a significant margin. A crowded Republican primary field of seven candidates is competing for the chance to face Soto in the general election on November 3, 2026.",
